[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue with one fix queued. Its reports, read one by
one, show three problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row below. The other two keep arriving after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {filed} />

- **parser** ([ticket](https://github.com/Badr4u/what-it-shows/issues/1)): the shared parser reads
  every date month first, and every tenant on file writes the day first. Day and month swap.
- **hint** ([ticket](https://github.com/Badr4u/what-it-shows/issues/2)): the booking-v3 form prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, people type month first as told, and the form reads it day
  first. Same symptom, different code, only through the form of booking-v3 tenants.
- **shift** ([ticket](https://github.com/Badr4u/what-it-shows/issues/3)): the date moves by one day,
  or two people in different time zones see different days. Nothing is swapped. The desk had
  already noted these as one-day moves, but the table filed them under the parser.

## How it was read

- One report, one count: the export repeats reports across its pages, so every count here is by
  unique id.
- The cause comes from the report's tenant and channel, and from what its body says. It does not
  come from the subject line or from intake's tag. Every subject used in #4471 shows up under more
  than one cause, and intake tags by the reporter's browser, so the "tagged as" column disagrees
  with the cause.
- Every body was read, not sampled. The swaps read as swaps; the one-day moves read as one-day moves.

## What to change on the desk

- Merging on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) is how three
  problems became one ticket. A new decision record should replace it; this page does not edit 0001.
- Before a big ticket is marked known, check its cause table. More than one row means more than one
  ticket.

